PASS [quaternionic QT] the face on the quaternionic span of two orthonormal vectors spans the corner Herm_2(H): real dimension 6, a 5-dimensional state ball of capacity 2: FP-S holds in HQT
PASS [classical] the face generated by k vertices of a simplex is a (k-1)-simplex (capacity k): FP-S, FP-O hold
PASS [square gbit] the states with zero last outcome of a complete measurement form an edge of capacity 2 (MM requires 1); the edge (dim 1) and the square (dim 2) have equal capacity 2 and are not affinely isomorphic: the subspace axiom (FP-S with FP-E) fails
PASS [K2-only theory] capacity 3 is not a power of 2: the 3-face of Q_2 is carried by no system, FP-S fails
PASS [real QT] phaseGate 0 = diag(i, 1) has non-real entry i: DrivesElementary at Fin 2 fails in RQT

VERDICT  complex QT satisfies FP-S, FP-O, FP-T and FP-C on every tested frame (n <= 6); real QT satisfies FP-S, FP-O, FP-T and fails the span form of FP-C; HQT and classical theory satisfy FP-S; the square gbit and the K2-only theory fail FP-S/FP-E
